{
  "requirement": "For node reads, the SDK constructs a `Snapshot` from\nthe contents returned by `Domain::node_content` and their\n`NodeContents::fingerprint` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`, without another read.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n\nimpl<T> Snapshot<T> {\n    pub fn new(content: T, fingerprint: Fingerprint) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<T: Clone> Clone for Snapshot<T>;\nimpl<T: Debug> Debug for Snapshot<T>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations in `requirements.sdk.graph.snapshot`**\n1. A node read builds a `Snapshot` from the contents returned by `Domain::node_content`.\n2. The snapshot's fingerprint is `NodeContents::fingerprint` of those same retained contents. This is the cited `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`.\n3. The read happens only once. There is no further read.\n4. `Snapshot<T>` has public `content` and `fingerprint` fields and a `Snapshot::new(content, fingerprint)` constructor.\n5. `Snapshot<T>` is `#[non_exhaustive]` and implements `Clone` and `Debug`.\n\n**Test coverage**\n- **Content and fingerprint from a node read.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` calls `read_snapshot`. It covers an empty string and large multi-byte Unicode content.\n  - It asserts that `snapshot.content.format()` equals the original and that `snapshot.fingerprint` equals `fp(original)`.\n  - It then replaces the underlying content and asserts the snapshot content is unchanged. It also asserts there are exactly two reads for two calls.\n- **Fingerprint comes from the retained contents, with no re-read.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` changes the content after the read.\n  - It asserts `snapshot.content.fingerprint() == snapshot.fingerprint`. It asserts the fingerprint value is still `\"before\"` and the content still formats as `\"before\"`.\n  - It asserts the read log is `[1]`. A fingerprint recomputed from a fresh read would show `\"after\"` or add a read, so the test rejects it.\n- **Exactly one read per call.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` clears the read log. It then calls `read`, `read_snapshot`, a second `read` after the content changes, and a failing read. It asserts the log is `[1,1,1,2]`.\n- **Fingerprint distinct per version.** The same test asserts `read_snapshot(...).fingerprint == fp(\"before\")`. It asserts the recorded dependencies keep the distinct `before` and `after` fingerprints.\n- **Real-domain check.** `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` checks that a retained node's fingerprint is stable after the underlying file changes. It also checks that `domain.node_content(..).fingerprint()` matches the one retained by `ctx.read`.\n- **Agent-tool node reads.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` asserts that the dependency recorded for a `read_node` tool call carries the fingerprint of the content read.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` asserts the same for the node-content dependencies it records. Its reads are `[1,3,2,3,1]`, one per insertion.\n- **Constructor and fields.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[callers_can_pair_content_with_its_fingerprint]` is an external-crate test. It builds a snapshot with `Snapshot::new` and asserts both public fields hold the supplied values. This also shows the public constructor works from outside the crate.\n- **`Clone`, `Debug`, `#[non_exhaustive]`.** I read `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#struct[Snapshot]`. It uses `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]` and `#[non_exhaustive]`. These are declarative derives and attributes with no conditional or transformation of their own, so no test is required. `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` also checks the public surface against the book.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets]` concerns edge snapshots, which are outside the \"node reads\" scope of this requirement.\n\n**Gaps:** none found. No acknowledgments (`{fixme}`) apply.",
